<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Swampy Lakes and Flagline Trails</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:267-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.999772" lon="-121.663687"><ele>1935.4</ele><name>Dutchman Flat Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:dutchman-flat-sno-park (OSM way 559496151); confidence: high; pdf_page: 269; book_elev_ft: 6400; quote: From Dutchman Flat Nordic Sno-Park, ski the trail north along the east edge of the open flat</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.024312" lon="-121.657374"><ele>2022.3</ele><name>Flagline Access / Flagline Trail #41 junction (map 60: trail 6 meets the Swampy Lks - Flagline trail)</name><desc>source: OSM node 1067700935 shared by Flagline Access XC trail 40.1 (way 294603184) and Flagline Trail #41 (way 299566182); 0.5 mi west of Tumalo Pass as map 60 draws; confidence: high; pdf_page: 269; quote: then enter old growth to the trail that connects Little Meadow with Tumalo Pass. Turn right (east) here 2 miles from the sno-park, and ski 0.5 mile to the flat pass</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.024798" lon="-121.650744"><ele>2058.4</ele><name>Tumalo Pass (6,750 ft saddle on the Flagline Trail)</name><desc>source: OSM Flagline Trail #41 node 3035457211 where the trail reaches 6,750 ft (DEM) 0.8 mi east of the Big Meadow junction, at the saddle north of Tumalo Mountain; today's trail then turns south and climbs over a 6,960 ft shoulder the book does not mention; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 269; book_elev_ft: 6750; quote: Turn right (east) here 2 miles from the sno-park, and ski 0.5 mile to the flat pass through alternating open swales and small meadows</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.007492" lon="-121.587553"><ele>1797.7</ele><name>Flagline Trail #41 meets Swampy Lakes Trail #23</name><desc>source: OSM node shared by Flagline Trail #41 (way 878847233) and Swampy Lakes Trail #23 (way 279479053); confidence: high; pdf_page: 269; quote: The last mile to the Swampy Lakes Shelter ... features a widely cleared trail with many long, smooth downhill runs</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.989467" lon="-121.568160"><ele>1769.6</ele><name>Swampy Lakes Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead th:swampy-lakes-sno-park (OSM relation 11960476); confidence: high; pdf_page: 273; book_elev_ft: 5700; quote: From the Swampy Lakes Shelter cross the open flat, climb the ridge, and descend to the sno-park where your car shuttle is waiting.</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Swampy Lakes and Flagline Trails</name><desc>1. Dutchman Flat Sno-Park -&gt; Flagline Access / Flagline Trail #41 junction (map 60: trail 6 meets the Swampy Lks - Flagline trail): osm (high), 2.16 mi | 2. Flagline Access / Flagline Trail #41 junction (map 60: trail 6 meets the Swampy Lks - Flagline trail) -&gt; Tumalo Pass (6,750 ft saddle on the Flagline Trail): osm (high), 0.38 mi | 3. Tumalo Pass (6,750 ft saddle on the Flagline Trail) -&gt; Flagline Trail #41 meets Swampy Lakes Trail #23: osm (high), 4.63 mi | 4. Flagline Trail #41 meets Swampy Lakes Trail #23 -&gt; Swampy Lakes Sno-Park: osm (high), 1.97 mi</desc>
